silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_27_governance_shacl_deep_dive_sections_03_unified_constraint_theorem_concrete_anchor_3#unifiedcongruence silm:hasLongDescription "The UnifiedCongruence is the joint congruence: the smallest congruence containing both governance-gate relators and SHACL-shape relators. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'UnifiedCongruence', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
